  "body": "There's an [old test](http://w3c-test.org/2dcontext/fill-and-stroke-styles/2d.fillStyle.parse.current.notrendered.html) ([git](https://github.com/w3c/web-platform-tests/blob/dccaa413ec1107e87b72245aa5ce837ee37ddff7/2dcontext/fill-and-stroke-styles/2d.fillStyle.parse.current.notrendered.html)) that checks that \"currentColor is computed from the canvas element even when element is not rendered\". The spec seems to require using transparent black for that case now.\n\nIt seems that Chrome, Firefox and Safari all pass the test as it is now; Edge uses transparent black.\n",
